A completed technical change can still leave the compliance story out of date.

Use a documentation-impact review after changes to systems, providers, roles, data flows, or operating procedures:
- update affected diagrams and boundaries;
- confirm implementation statements still match reality;
- revise procedures and responsible roles;
- check shared-responsibility assignments;
- link the new operational records;
- record who reviewed the updates.

Cloud2e’s CMMC documentation service focuses on aligning the SSP, policies, procedures, shared responsibility matrix, and operational evidence with the environment they describe. This helps organizations replace conflicting documents and optimistic templates with documentation tied to actual work.

The useful question is not just, “Did the change succeed?” It is also, “Did every document and record that depends on it remain accurate?”

